msgid "IDS_ADECK_ONBOARDING_COMPLETE_TEXT_P1"
msgstr ""
"May 1940. France. The situation on the front had taken a dire turn for the "
"Allies. By May 20, large numbers of British, French, and Belgian troops had "
"been pushed back to the sea near Dunkirk. In response, the British Admiralty"
" launched an evacuation operation to rescue the soldiers, setting a historic"
" precedent. On the first day, May 26, several dozen ships participated in "
"the operation."

