msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNB076_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The idea of using artillery on ships goes back to antiquity—as far back as "
"Gaius Julius Caesar, who wrote about the use of ship catapults in the Gallic"
" War. Byzantine dromes were also equipped with flamethrowers and catapults. "
"Since the Middle Ages, warships have been equipped with cannons of various "
"calibers. Initially, ships carried stern and bow guns that were primarily "
"used for bombarding structures on land. Later, onboard cannons were "
"developed for naval combat against enemy ships."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNB076_NAME"
msgstr "Artillery"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNB077_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For participating in the Supertest."

