msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP001_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Raccoons are mammals that originate from North America. According to indigenous mythology, the raccoon is frequently associated with the role of a trickster and is believed to possess supernatural abilities due to its distinctive facial coloring that resembles battle makeup.\n"
"\n"
"To commemorate the Jokes of Nature event."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP001_NAME"
msgstr "Raccoon"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP002_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Along with the club, knife, and axe, the spear was one of the first and most"
" important tools created by man. The spear has been used throughout history "
"for hunting and fishing. It has been used as a weapon in almost every "
"conflict in history right up to modern times, with it being retained even "
"today in the form of bayonets on rifles."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP002_NAME"
msgstr "Javelins"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP003_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The revolver is a firearm characterized by its short barrel and ability to "
"fire fast consecutive shots. It features a rotating drum with several "
"chambers, each loaded with a single cartridge. A true symbol of the Wild "
"West, the revolver eventually lost popularity to more convenient semi-"
"automatic pistols, but it is still used in sports and hunting."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP003_NAME"
msgstr "Revolver"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP004_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Macedonian-style shooting is the simultaneous use of two firearms, one in "
"each hand. Although this firing method is common in popular culture, it is "
"considered ineffective and is not typically used in practice."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP004_NAME"
msgstr "Two Barrels"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP005_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Bows and arrows were extensively employed by humans from ancient times until"
" the early modern era; however, their significance diminished with the "
"advent of more potent and precise firearms. Today, bows are mainly used for "
"hunting and sports."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP005_NAME"
msgstr "Bow"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP006_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The battle hammer was most commonly used in the late Middle Ages when modern"
" armor became so strong that it was difficult to penetrate with swords and "
"axes—they just rebounded off. On the other hand, the hammer could inflict "
"significant damage on the enemy because its striking power did not need to "
"penetrate armor."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP006_NAME"
msgstr "Hammer"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP007_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Thank you for your contribution to our community!"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP007_NAME"
msgstr "Contributor"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP008_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Admiral William Halsey became one of the contributors to the Allied victory in the Pacific.\n"
"\n"
"A commemorative symbol issued for finishing the \"Hit hard! Hit fast! Hit often!\" campaign."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP008_NAME"
msgstr "Admiral Halsey"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP009_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Sport is essentially the spirit of irreconcilable competition, a battle "
"between the most ambitious competitors dedicated to the end. But, at the "
"same time, sport unites people and creates true bonds of friendship."

