msgstr "Keel Breaker"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP057_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Every year, on November 11, the U.S. honors those who served in the U.S. "
"Armed Forces. This holiday was originally established as Reconciliation Day "
"to commemorate the end of hostilities in World War I, but it was then "
"renamed Veterans Day in 1954."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP057_NAME"
msgstr "Veterans Day"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP058_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The history of the Polish Navy dates back to the 15th century, but the "
"modern Polish Navy was founded only after World War I."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP058_NAME"
msgstr "100th Anniversary of the Polish Navy"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP059_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"To commemorate the bravery of the Czechoslovakian Legions and their "
"important role in founding the independent Czechoslovakian Republic in 1918."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP059_NAME"
msgstr "Czechoslovakian Legions"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP060_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In commemoration of the \"Victory\" competition."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP060_NAME"
msgstr "Victory"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP061_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In commemoration of the \"Victory\" competition."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP061_NAME"
msgstr "Honor"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP062_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In commemoration of the \"Victory\" competition."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP062_NAME"
msgstr "Glory"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP063_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For valuable contributions to the game and community."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP063_NAME"
msgstr "Privateer"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP064_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For taking part in the Public Test Summer Marathon."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP064_NAME"
msgstr "PT Summer Season"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP065_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The history of the U.S. Navy traces its roots back to the War of "
"Independence. On October 13, 1775, the Second Continental Congress "
"authorized the purchase of two ships, marking an important step in the "
"establishment of the Navy. In 1794, Congress ordered the construction of six"
" three-masted frigates. Today, USS Constitution—one of those ships—is the "
"oldest vessel that remains afloat in the world. The frigate is still listed "
"as part of the fleet."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP065_NAME"
msgstr "Birthday of the U.S. Navy"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP066_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The history of the United States Marine Corps begins with two battalions "
"formed on November 10, 1775, in Philadelphia. The new branch of the armed "
"forces was designed to perform combat missions both at sea and ashore."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP066_NAME"
msgstr "Birthday of the U.S. Marines"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP067_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The name of Japanese destroyer Asashio translates as \"Morning Tide.\" "
"Asashio entered service in 1937 as the lead ship of an entire class of "
"destroyers, and she sank during the Battle of the Bismarck Sea in March "
"1943."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP067_NAME"
msgstr "Asashio"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP068_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Japanese heavy cruiser Atago was named after a mountain located near Kyoto, "
"which holds one of the most revered Shinto shrines atop it."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP068_NAME"
msgstr "Atago"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP069_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The famous German inventor and airship designer, Ferdinand von Zeppelin, "
"came from an old noble family. The Zeppelin estates were situated in "
"Mecklenburg and Pomerania, and the family coat of arms depicts a donkey's "
"head facing right."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP069_NAME"
msgstr "Graf Zeppelin"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP070_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The coat of arms of Prussian General Gerhard von Scharnhorst, who became a "
"national hero during the German War of Liberation of 1813. Both ships of the"
" Scharnhorst class, named in his honor, bore the same coat of arms."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP070_NAME"
msgstr "Scharnhorst"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP071_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Admiral William Sims is one of the main Navy reformers whose efforts in the "
"first decades of the 20th century allowed the U.S. Navy to stand on par with"
" the most powerful navies of the world at that time. In 1939, a destroyer "
"named after the admiral was commissioned as the lead ship in a series of "
"12 ships."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP071_NAME"
msgstr "USS Sims"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP072_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The heaviest European Battleship ever made, this ship raided convoys and was"
" a feared vessel in the Arctic and Atlantic oceans."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP072_NAME"
msgstr "Tirpitz"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP073_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Submarines proved their combat effectiveness and earned their status as a "
"formidable weapon in paving the way to victory as far back as the early 20th"
" century."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP073_NAME"
msgstr "Stealthy Threat"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP074_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Your undivided attention contributes to the high quality of our game "
"updates!"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP074_NAME"
msgstr "CST Participant"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP075_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For taking part in the Public Test Autumn Marathon."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP075_NAME"
msgstr "PT Autumn Season"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP076_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For taking part in the Public Test Winter Marathon."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP076_NAME"
msgstr "PT Winter Season"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP077_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For taking part in the Public Test Spring Marathon."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP077_NAME"
msgstr "PT Spring Season"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP078_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Located at the Muskogee War Memorial, SS-310 served valiantly in World War "
"II and earned six battle stars plus a Presidential Unit Citation in service "
"of her country."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP078_NAME"
msgstr "USS Batfish"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP079_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Battle of Friday the 13th, which took place in November 1942, proved "
"fatal for light cruiser Atlanta. However, two years after the ship's "
"destruction, USS Atlanta \"rose from the ashes\" like the city the ship was "
"named after. Thus, in December 1944, a new cruiser bearing this glorious "
"name entered service."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP079_NAME"
msgstr "USS Atlanta"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP080_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Commissioned in 1938, HMS Cossack earned fame in World War II under the "
"command of Philip Vian during the Altmark incident, the Battle of Narvik, "
"and the hunt for Bismarck."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP080_NAME"
msgstr "HMS Cossack"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP081_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Several French Navy ships carried the name of the legendary Dunkirk corsair "
"Jean Bart, who brought glory to himself in all the naval wars led by France "
"in the late 17th century. One such ship to take his name was a Richelieu-"
"class battleship commissioned in 1949."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP081_NAME"
msgstr "Jean Bart"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP082_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Dedicated to the U.S. Navy of the World War era."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP082_NAME"
msgstr "Wings"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP083_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Dedicated to the U.S. Navy of the World War era."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP083_NAME"
msgstr "Stars"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP084_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Dedicated to the U.S. Navy of the World War era."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP084_NAME"
msgstr "Stars 'n' Stripes"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP085_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Lest We Forget"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP085_NAME"
msgstr "Remembrance Day"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP086_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Military equipment for battles on any planet. Designed for a wide range of "
"tactical situations."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP086_NAME"
msgstr "Seatek Corporation"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP087_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Military equipment based on unfathomable alien scientific developments. The "
"most mysterious of all space corporations."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP087_NAME"
msgstr "Phobos Corporation"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP088_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Military equipment for battles on the most distant planets. Corporate "
"management is well known for its unscrupulousness."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP088_NAME"
msgstr "Pelamida Corporation"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP089_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Sea beast created with the aid of the most complex extraterrestrial "
"technologies."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP089_NAME"
msgstr "Monsters"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP090_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Kimchi holds a special place in Korean national cuisine; it is eaten as a "
"side dish with almost anything. There are hundreds of types of kimchi. "
"Salted and pickled vegetables, seasoned with hot spices, are used to make "
"it. In the past, this dish was stored in clay pots that were partially "
"buried in the ground. It helped store it during winters and slow down the "
"fermentation process during summers. Nowadays, there are special "
"refrigerators for kimchi."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP090_NAME"
msgstr "Kimchi"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP091_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In ancient times, the main purpose of lighthouses was to indicate entrances "
"to ports. One of the Seven Wonders of the World, the Pharos of Alexandria, "
"was destroyed by a series of earthquakes between 956 and 1323 AD. Modern "
"lighthouses appeared at the beginning of the 18th century, and the demand "
"for them increased due to the development of transatlantic trade. The "
"purpose of lighthouses has gradually changed since then: They now warn of "
"dangerous coasts, shallows, reefs, and rocks, as well as facilitate "
"navigation."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP091_NAME"
msgstr "Lighthouse"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP092_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "To celebrate the Verizon Warrior's Championship."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP092_NAME"
msgstr "Verizon Warrior's Championship"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP093_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For participants of Copa Latina-Americana Warships."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP093_NAME"
msgstr "Copa Latina-Americana Warships"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP094_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For the glorious winners of Copa Latina-Americana Warships."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP094_NAME"
msgstr "Copa Latina-Americana Warships Winner"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP095_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For the MVPs of Copa Latina-Americana Warships."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP095_NAME"
msgstr "Copa Latina-Americana Warships MVP"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP096_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The High Seas Fleet War Badge of the Kriegsmarine was awarded to the "
"personnel of battleships and cruisers for their service on the high seas. "
"Those who survived when Bismarck sank were among the first to receive this "
"reward."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP096_NAME"
msgstr "The Hunt for Bismarck"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP097_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In the entire history of the Royal Navy so far, 15 ships have been named "
"Tiger. From 1944 to 1945, three cruisers that were being built shared that "
"name. This Tiger entered service in 1959, and her side number was C20."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP097_NAME"
msgstr "HMS Tiger"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP098_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"After the fall of the monarchy in Germany in 1919, the Weimar Constitution "
"declared Germany a republic. It was suggested that the flag of the navy be "
"replaced with a new state eagle and the Iron Cross, but this idea was "
"rejected."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP098_NAME"
msgstr "Weimar"

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP099_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Sport is essentially the spirit of irreconcilable competition, a battle "
"between the most ambitious competitors who are dedicated to the end. But, at"
" the same time, sport unites people and creates true bonds of friendship."

msgid "IDS_DOGTAG_PCNP099_NAME"
msgstr "Austria"

