msgstr "Go to the event screen"

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_1_PAGE_1_PARAGRAPH_1"
msgstr ""
"Transport ships will only move forward under your protection. Stay within "
"the escort zone to ensure their advance."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_1_PAGE_1_PARAGRAPH_2"
msgstr ""
"If left unguarded, the transport ship will halt, becoming an easier target "
"for enemy attacks."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_1_PAGE_1_TITLE_1"
msgstr "Transport Ship Escort"

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_1_PAGE_2_PARAGRAPH_1"
msgstr ""
"Minefields pose a serious threat to transport ships. Once deployed, their "
"zones appear both in the combat zone and on the Minimap."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_1_PAGE_2_PARAGRAPH_2"
msgstr ""
"Use depth charges to destroy minefields, but be cautious—mines are often "
"tightly grouped and can detonate in sequence, causing damage."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_1_PAGE_2_TITLE_1"
msgstr "Minefields"

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_2_PAGE_1_PARAGRAPH_1"
msgstr ""
"During night battles, flares and burning wrecks light up the sea and "
"gradually fade. Any ship entering these illuminated areas becomes "
"significantly easier to detect. Steer clear to reduce the risk of exposure."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_2_PAGE_1_PARAGRAPH_2"
msgstr "The illuminated areas are indicated on the Minimap and Tactical Map."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_2_PAGE_1_TITLE_1"
msgstr "Illuminated Areas"

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_2_PAGE_2_PARAGRAPH_1"
msgstr ""
"During night battles, ships and aircraft are harder to detect. Firing main "
"guns increases your detectability up to the maximum range of the main guns."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_2_PAGE_2_PARAGRAPH_2"
msgstr ""
"At night, detectability resets faster than in daytime battles, making ships "
"harder to spot."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_2_PAGE_2_TITLE_1"
msgstr "Night Conditions"

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_3_PAGE_1_PARAGRAPH_1"
msgstr ""
"To capture an island, you must first neutralize the enemy's coastal guns."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_3_PAGE_1_PARAGRAPH_2"
msgstr ""
"Once the coastal battery is neutralized, wait for USS San Diego to arrive. A"
" Key Area will appear—capture it together with San Diego."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_3_PAGE_1_PARAGRAPH_3"
msgstr ""
"Captured Areas cannot be recaptured by the enemy. After securing an island, "
"a new objective will appear. Proceed to capture it."

msgid "IDS_EVENT_WIKI_WW2OPERATIONS_TAB_3_PAGE_1_TITLE_1"
msgstr "Island Hopping"

