msgid "IDS_NARRATIVE_CAMPAIGN_CHAPTER_DESCRIPTION_C0"
msgstr ""
"The first major clash between British troops and Patriot militias took place on April 19, 1775, at Lexington and Concord.\n"
"\n"
"David Clark, a young man who joined the militia to fight for freedom, recounts his experience at North Bridge and his first impressions of the war in letters to his mother."

msgid "IDS_NARRATIVE_CAMPAIGN_CHAPTER_DESCRIPTION_C1"
msgstr ""
"The Continental Army's first major victory came at Saratoga on October 7, 1777, when British General John Burgoyne surrendered.\n"
"\n"
"In an unofficial report to a fellow officer and friend in the Province of Quebec, British Major Jonathan Harris reflects on the aftermath and how it changed him."

msgid "IDS_NARRATIVE_CAMPAIGN_CHAPTER_DESCRIPTION_C2"
msgstr ""
"The war went global when France joined as an ally. With the French fleet now engaged, American and French forces took the fight to sea.\n"
"\n"
"André Bernard, a French sailor, later wrote to a friend about how the experience changed what he thought war and glory meant."

msgid "IDS_NARRATIVE_CAMPAIGN_CHAPTER_DESCRIPTION_C3"
msgstr ""
"The Siege of Yorktown was the decisive victory of the war, shifting the conflict toward negotiations. Two years later, the Treaty of Paris recognized the independence of the United States.\n"
"\n"
"In his memoir, painter Edward Mercer describes witnessing the moments that shaped a new nation."

