msgid "IDS_PASB918"
msgstr "AL Massachusetts"

msgid "IDS_PASB918_DESCR"
msgstr ""
"The third battleship of the South Dakota class. Compared to her serious and straightforward sister, South Dakota, she has a more carefree personality. Though she has a muscle-brained, physically oriented way of thinking, her strength also fuels her desire to protect others. She tends to handle tough things on her own.\n"
"From the Azur Lane game."

msgid "IDS_PASB918_FULL"
msgstr "AL Massachusetts"

msgid "IDS_PASB918_NUMBER"
msgstr "4"

msgid "IDS_PASB918_YEAR"
msgstr "1942"

msgid "IDS_PASB919"
msgstr "Iowa 2"

msgid "IDS_PASB919_DESCR"
msgstr ""
"The Iowa-class battleships, among the most formidable representatives of "
"their ship type globally, were designed to support and safeguard high-speed "
"aircraft carrier formations. The lifting of international restrictions paved"
" the way for the creation of ships with robust protection and formidable "
"armament. USS Iowa took part in numerous World War II operations, including "
"the Battles of the Philippine Sea and Leyte Gulf. She also supported UN "
"forces during the Korean War. The battleship is currently moored in the Port"
" of Los Angeles as a museum ship."

msgid "IDS_PASB919_FULL"
msgstr "Iowa 2"

msgid "IDS_PASB919_NUMBER"
msgstr "6"

msgid "IDS_PASB919_YEAR"
msgstr "1943"

msgid "IDS_PASB920"
msgstr "Montana 2"

msgid "IDS_PASB920_DESCR"
msgstr ""
"The Montana-class ships were an evolution of the Iowa-class \"fast "
"battleships\": They were larger, better armored, and more heavily armed. The"
" main armament was expanded to include twelve 406 mm guns arranged in four "
"triple-gun turrets. The preliminary design work had commenced even before "
"the United States entered World War II. The attack on Pearl Harbor delayed "
"construction, and the success of aircraft carriers in the Battle of the "
"Coral Sea and Battle of Midway prompted the U.S. to opt against pursuing the"
" Montana class in favor of more promising ship types."

msgid "IDS_PASB920_FULL"
msgstr "Montana 2"

msgid "IDS_PASB920_NUMBER"
msgstr "0"

msgid "IDS_PASB920_YEAR"
msgstr "1941"

msgid "IDS_PASB930"
