msgid "IDS_PCEE004_MOONCAKE_FLAG"
msgstr "Mooncake"

msgid "IDS_PCEE004_MOONCAKE_FLAG_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Mooncakes are traditional Chinese pastries eaten during the Mid-Autumn "
"Festival, one of the most important celebrations in China. Centered on "
"harvest and family reunion, the festival is also linked to moon worship and "
"the legend of Chang'e, the Moon Goddess."

msgid "IDS_PCEE004_MOONCAKE_FLAG_EXTRA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In honor of the Mid-Autumn Festival."

msgid "IDS_PCEE005_IDME_REFRESH_FLAG"
msgstr "Warships Salute"

msgid "IDS_PCEE005_IDME_REFRESH_FLAG_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Raise this flag in celebration of the U.S. Navy's 250th anniversary and in "
"tribute to all who have served, past and present."

msgid "IDS_PCEE006_BDAY10_FLAG"
msgstr "A Decade at Sea"

msgid "IDS_PCEE006_BDAY10_FLAG_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Ten years at sea is an outstanding milestone for any commander. Over the "
"years, the game has been filled with countless events, thrilling battles, "
"new mechanics, remarkable achievements, ups and downs, and, most "
"importantly, the unforgettable memories it brings. All this has shaped World"
" of Warships into the game we know and love today. Endless horizons of new "
"adventures await!"

msgid "IDS_PCEE006_BDAY10_FLAG_EXTRA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "To celebrate World of Warships' Tenth Anniversary."

msgid "IDS_PCEE007_SIBIR_FLAG"
msgstr "Sibir"

msgid "IDS_PCEE007_SIBIR_FLAG_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The vast region of Siberia (\"Sibir\" in Russian) became a major target of "
"industrialization by the Soviet government in the 1930s. During the Great "
"Patriotic War, it gained even greater importance as a secure rear base for "
"the wartime economy. Thousands of citizens from this region also served in "
"the Red Army as fierce and skilled soldiers and marksmen."

msgid "IDS_PCEE008_RANK20"
msgstr "The Third League"

msgid "IDS_PCEE008_RANK20_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Flag of the Third League."

msgid "IDS_PCEE009_RANK10"
msgstr "The Second League"

msgid "IDS_PCEE009_RANK10_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Flag of the Second League."

msgid "IDS_PCEE010_RANK1"
msgstr "The First League"

msgid "IDS_PCEE010_RANK1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Flag of the First League."

msgid "IDS_PCEE011_SEASONFLAG01"
msgstr "Port of Kure"

msgid "IDS_PCEE011_SEASONFLAG01_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In the former Empire of Japan, an Imperial Navy base was located in Kure, "
"and this is where Yamato—one of the two largest battleships in World War "
"II—was built."

msgid "IDS_PCEE011_SEASONFLAG01_EXTRA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For achieving Rank 14 in Ranked Battles Season 2 (old)."

msgid "IDS_PCEE012_SEASONFLAG02"
msgstr "Jolly Roger"

msgid "IDS_PCEE012_SEASONFLAG02_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This flag, alongside dozens of other flags, was used by pirates in the 17th "
"and 18th centuries. While there was never a unified pirate flag, the symbol "
"of the skull and crossbones has been closely associated with piracy from the"
" 19th century until the modern day."

msgid "IDS_PCEE012_SEASONFLAG02_EXTRA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For achieving Rank 1 in Ranked Battles (old)."

msgid "IDS_PCEE013_SEASONFLAG03"
msgstr "Hawaii"

msgid "IDS_PCEE013_SEASONFLAG03_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In 1889, the U.S. Navy established a naval base in Pearl Harbor, Hawaii. On "
"December 7, 1941, the base was attacked by Japanese naval aviation and "
"midget submarines, bringing the United States fully into World War II."

msgid "IDS_PCEE013_SEASONFLAG03_EXTRA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For achieving Rank 14 in Ranked Battles Season 3 (old)."

