msgid "IDS_PCZC1099_AZURLANE_8_3_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "You know, you can always count on Baltimore."

msgid "IDS_PCZC109_NY2018_SCHARNHORST_RADAR"
msgstr "Scharnhorst's Forward Radar Set"

msgid "IDS_PCZC109_NY2018_SCHARNHORST_RADAR_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"At the beginning of 1942, Scharnhorst was equipped with new FuMO 27 radars. One set was fitted above the forward rangefinder tower located on top of the fore superstructure, and the other set was placed on the aft rangefinder tower. The 2 x 4 m mattress antenna rotated together with the rangefinder towers. These radars could detect an enemy ship at a distance of 25 km.\n"
"\n"
"However, during the Battle of the North Cape, the British ships surpassed Scharnhorst in both the quality and quantity of radar equipment. What's more, in an attempt to avoid detection, the radar systems on the Scharnhorst had been turned off. In doing so, Scharnhorst was unable to detect enemy ships in time. The first salvos fired by the British cruisers came as a total surprise to the German ship. One of the first hits crippled the forward FuMO 27 set. Under polar night conditions, Scharnhorst, blinded by the loss of her radar, fell right into the trap set by the British."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1100_AZURLANE_8_4_1"
msgstr "Pull the Reins in... on You"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1100_AZURLANE_8_4_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Chapayev: Look, Commander—You've got matching accessories!"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1101_AZURLANE_8_4_2"
msgstr "Watch and Learn"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1101_AZURLANE_8_4_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Belfast: Good evening. Would you like to assist?\n"
"\n"
"Neptune: Sure. Show me how it's done, Ms. Head Maid."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1102_AZURLANE_8_4_3"
msgstr "The Perfect Maid"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1102_AZURLANE_8_4_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Every duty handled with care."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1103_AZURLANE_8_4_4"
msgstr "Clingy"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1103_AZURLANE_8_4_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Cheshire: Meow? Owneeer! Squeeze! Cuddle!"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1104_AZURLANE_8_5_1"
msgstr "Fill 'Er Up"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1104_AZURLANE_8_5_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Marco Polo: The port was long overdue an expansion, so I took it upon myself to reclaim some land!\n"
"\n"
"Nicoloso da Recco: So... how are we gonna dock now?"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1105_AZURLANE_8_5_2"
msgstr "Hey, Commander"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1105_AZURLANE_8_5_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Pull up a chair!"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1106_AZURLANE_8_5_3"
msgstr "Model Modeler"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1106_AZURLANE_8_5_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Admiral Hipper: Pfft. This is nothing!\n"
"\n"
"Prinz Eugen: Impressive...\n"
"\n"
"Blücher: You're so skilled, Hipper!"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1107_AZURLANE_8_5_4"
msgstr "Daydreams Princessly"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1107_AZURLANE_8_5_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Gorizia: My knight in shining armor... (the Commander)"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1108_SABATON_1_1"
msgstr "Joakim Brodén"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1108_SABATON_1_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The voice of Sabaton, Joakim is known for his commanding stage presence, "
"signature sunglasses, unique voice, and defined vocals. His charisma shapes "
"much of the band's live energy."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1109_SABATON_1_2"
msgstr "Microphone"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1109_SABATON_1_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"More than just a tool—Joakim's mic is often treated like a weapon, a way to "
"project history and power into every corner of the stage."

msgid "IDS_PCZC110_NY2018_NORFOLKGK"
msgstr "Main Battery Turret of Cruiser Norfolk"

msgid "IDS_PCZC110_NY2018_NORFOLKGK_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"HMS Norfolk belonged to the third series of County-class heavy cruisers designed under the Washington Naval Treaty of 1922, which defined such cruisers as warships of up to 10,000 tons displacement carrying guns no larger than 8 inches (203 mm) in caliber. The ship's eight 8-inch (203 mm) guns were placed in Mk.II twin-gun turrets to make up one of the most efficient artillery systems of the time. It had high armor penetration capacity and great destructive power, sending four to five rounds per minute at a range of up to 28 km.\n"
"\n"
"At North Cape, HMS Norfolk was the first to successfully hit Scharnhorst at the outset of the battle. A lucky shot from the cruiser hit the German battleship's forward radar, resulting in what turned out to be catastrophic damage. Blinded by the loss of her radar, Scharnhorst sailed right into the trap set by the British."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1110_SABATON_1_3"
msgstr "Heroes"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1110_SABATON_1_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Joakim's favorite album.\n"
"\n"
"\"The first album recorded with the current line-up, featuring some of my personal favorite songs, while also including a couple of or most (in my opinion) underrated tracks. 'To Hell and Back' and 'Night Witches' lead the charge among fan favorites, while 'Hearts of Iron' and 'The Ballad of Bull' are often forgotten.\""

msgid "IDS_PCZC1111_SABATON_1_4"
msgstr "Signature Sunglasses"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1111_SABATON_1_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Perhaps the most iconic part of Joakim's look. The reflective shades have "
"become his armor, inseparable from his image on and off stage."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1112_SABATON_2_1"
msgstr "Pär Sundström"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1112_SABATON_2_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As bassist and co-founder, Pär anchors both the music and the management of "
"Sabaton. His dedication behind the scenes is as vital as his heavy bass "
"lines."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1113_SABATON_2_2"
msgstr "Bass Guitar"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1113_SABATON_2_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A low, rumbling force that drives the rhythm of Sabaton's songs, Pär's bass "
"is an essential weapon in the band's arsenal."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1114_SABATON_2_3"
msgstr "The Art of War"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1114_SABATON_2_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Pär's favorite album.\n"
"\n"
"\"It was the first try we made at a concept album, and it was a huge leap in production value from the earlier works. 'Ghost Division' is a fantastic song and never boring to play live, but my favorite songs from the album are 'Cliffs of Gallipoli' or 'The Price of a Mile'.\""

msgid "IDS_PCZC1115_SABATON_2_4"
msgstr "Setlist"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1115_SABATON_2_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A setlist is like a battle plan, and a lot of time is put into forging it to"
" ensure that fans get the best possible experience."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1116_SABATON_3_1"
msgstr "Chris Rörland"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1116_SABATON_3_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A guitarist with precision and passion, Chris brings Sabaton's melodies to "
"life with his sharp riffs and stage energy."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1117_SABATON_3_2"
msgstr "Guitar"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1117_SABATON_3_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A guitar with a custom finish and relentless power, Chris's guitar "
"symbolizes the heavy artillery of Sabaton's sound."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1118_SABATON_3_3"
msgstr "Legends"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1118_SABATON_3_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Chris's favorite album.\n"
"\n"
"\"To me, it feels like the most powerful statement we've ever made as a band. It captures not only the strength of the songwriting but also the unity and chemistry we've built together over the years. Tracks like 'Templars', 'A Tiger Among Dragons', 'Crossing the Rubicon', 'Lightning at the Gates', and 'Impaler' really showcase what we can create when we're at our very best. I believe 'Legends' will stand the test of time and be remembered as one of the greats.\""

msgid "IDS_PCZC1119_SABATON_3_4"
msgstr "Vinyl"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1119_SABATON_3_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Chris is a huge collector of vinyl records. His collection has been "
"described by other Sabaton members as legendary!"

msgid "IDS_PCZC111_NY2018_DUKEOFYORKEMBLEM"
msgstr "Badge of Battleship Duke of York"

msgid "IDS_PCZC111_NY2018_DUKEOFYORKEMBLEM_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"HMS Duke of York, a battleship of the King George V class, entered service in 1941. The ship's badge depicts a white rose—the heraldic symbol of the House of York and the Dukes of York—as well as elements and the Motto of the Order of the Garter that is regarded as the most prestigious British order.\n"
"\n"
"In December 1943, battleship Duke of York was the flagship of Vice Admiral Fraser, Commander of the Home Fleet, playing a crucial role in the destruction of German battleship Scharnhorst at the Battle of the North Cape."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1120_SABATON_4_1"
msgstr "Thobbe Englund"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1120_SABATON_4_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Returning to the band in 2024, Thobbe's fiery playing style and Viking-like "
"stage presence bring raw power to Sabaton's performances."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1121_SABATON_4_2"
msgstr "Guitar"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1121_SABATON_4_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Thobbe has stayed true to the classic electric guitar since before Sabaton "
"was formed. He is inseparable from his guitar to the point that it has "
"become part of him. Wherever you find Thobbe, rest assured that a Fender "
"Stratocaster is nearby."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1122_SABATON_4_3"
msgstr "Carolus Rex"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1122_SABATON_4_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Thobbe's favorite album.\n"
"\n"
"\"It contains solid heavy metal songs like 'The Lion From The North,' 'The Carolean's Prayer,' 'A Lifetime of War,' and of course the title track, which stand out to me as some of the greatest Sabaton songs. A solid and straightforward album. Wow!\""

msgid "IDS_PCZC1123_SABATON_4_4"
msgstr "Thobbe's Hand-Built Car"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1123_SABATON_4_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"When it comes to classic Swedish cars built with safety and longevity in "
"mind, Thobbe Englund knows them inside out—so much so that he actually built"
" one entirely from original factory components. Sitting inside feels like "
"stepping into a time machine: even the seat belts carry handwritten tags "
"from 1979, signed by the workers who assembled and tested them."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1124_SABATON_5_1"
msgstr "Hannes Van Dahl"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1124_SABATON_5_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Behind the kit since 2013, Hannes drives Sabaton’s unstoppable rhythm, known"
" for his stamina and explosive live energy."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1125_SABATON_5_2"
msgstr "Drum Kit"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1125_SABATON_5_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Massive. Hannes' kick drums hit like naval cannons in arenas. As the "
"backbone of the band, he is as reliable as a machine."

msgid "IDS_PCZC1126_SABATON_5_3"
msgstr "The War to End All Wars"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1126_SABATON_5_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Hannes's favorite album.\n"
"\n"
"\"'The War to End All Wars,' and I don't necessarily know why. It's just a feeling. That whole period—and to get and play that record on that tour—was awesome, the way it developed as a kind of younger brother to 'The Great War'. Everything from the mix to the songs and the tour!! Awesome memories!! That being said, I can’t wait for what 'Legends' will bring!!\""

msgid "IDS_PCZC1127_SABATON_5_4"
msgstr "Photographs"

msgid "IDS_PCZC1127_SABATON_5_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Hannes is a huge fan of photography and is often seen taking photos of "
"everything! Not a day passes without Hannes taking photos. Humans, animals, "
"buildings, or tanks—everything is captured in his lens, on and off tours."

