msgid "IDS_PCZC113_NY2018_SAUMAREZEMBLEM"
msgstr "Badge of Destroyer Saumarez"

msgid "IDS_PCZC113_NY2018_SAUMAREZEMBLEM_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"HMS Saumarez, commissioned in 1943, was an S-Class Flotilla Leader that served with the 5th Emergency Flotilla of destroyers designed specifically for operations in the Arctic waters. The ship was named after a prominent British naval commander of the 18–19th centuries.\n"
"\n"
"In December 1943, Saumarez, along with three other same-class destroyers, operated within the Distant Cover Force escorting the JW 55B and RA 55A convoys. The ship took part in a torpedo attack on Scharnhorst and, despite losses in men and damage to the ship, Saumarez fired four of her torpedoes from a range of about 1,600 m, expecting, along with HMS Savage, to score two to three hits in total."

