msgid "IDS_PCZC919_STAR_TREK_1_1"
msgstr "Borg Cube"

msgid "IDS_PCZC919_STAR_TREK_1_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Borg powerhouse, pinnacle of the Collective's advancement, and one of the most formidable craft to have ever roamed space—the Borg cube can reach approximately three kilometers in length and accommodate a crew of countless drones. Transwarp-capable and possessing a vast array of weapons, this spaceship can destroy or assimilate almost anything in its path.\n"
"\n"
"In the Battle of Wolf 359, the Borg demonstrated their ruthless power, leaving Starfleet on the brink of devastating defeat, as one Borg cube managed to destroy almost every ship in the fleet. The aftermath of this battle prompted the United Federation of Planets to urgently develop strategies to repel future Borg assaults."

msgid "IDS_PCZC920_STAR_TREK_1_2"
msgstr "U.S.S. Enterprise-D"

msgid "IDS_PCZC920_STAR_TREK_1_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The U.S.S. Enterprise-D, pride of Starfleet and a symbol of exploration. Launched in 2363, this Galaxy-class starship was outfitted for both diplomatic and combat missions, featuring advanced technology and powerful weaponry.\n"
"\n"
"Throughout its daring voyages under Captain Jean-Luc Picard, the Enterprise-D faced countless challenges—including the terrifying Borg—repeatedly demonstrating the resilience and bravery of her crew. The Enterprise-D embodies the Federation's enduring quest for peace."

msgid "IDS_PCZC921_STAR_TREK_1_3"
msgstr "Romulan Warbird"

msgid "IDS_PCZC921_STAR_TREK_1_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Romulan D'deridex-class Warbirds are powerful and intimidating starships. Their massive, double-hulled design is more than twice the size of a Galaxy-class craft. Equipped with one of the most advanced cloaking systems in the galaxy, the Warbird can easily evade sensors, launch surprise attacks, and excel in stealth missions.\n"
"\n"
"Unique artificial quantum singularity drive, together with disruptors and plasma torpedoes, allows the Warbird to deliver devastating firepower."

msgid "IDS_PCZC923_STAR_TREK_1_4"
msgstr "Negh'Var"

msgid "IDS_PCZC923_STAR_TREK_1_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Negh'Var is a powerful Klingon warship known for being one of the largest and most formidable cruiser classes in the Klingon Defense Force. IKS Negh'Var served as flagship for the Klingon Empire.\n"
"\n"
"Heavily armed with disruptors, photon torpedoes, and powerful shields, the Negh'Var embodies the Klingons' fierce warrior spirit, exemplifying the military philosophy of their empire. The imposing design and advanced technology make it a symbol of Klingon might."

msgid "IDS_PCZC924_STAR_TREK_2_1"
msgstr "Borg Sphere"

msgid "IDS_PCZC924_STAR_TREK_2_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Borg long-range tactical vessel, known as the Borg sphere, was engineered for specialized operations, such as scouting and escort missions. These vessels are significantly smaller than Borg cubes but no less forbidding. Some spheres are housed within larger cubes, sharing their design and advanced systems. Equipped with an array of Borg weaponry and technologies—including a powerful tractor beam—the spheres can immobilize their targets before assimilation.\n"
"\n"
"One of the most infamous spheres was the Borg Queen's Sphere, which played a major role during the Borg's attempt to assimilate Earth in 2373."

msgid "IDS_PCZC925_STAR_TREK_2_2"
msgstr "Planet Romulus"

msgid "IDS_PCZC925_STAR_TREK_2_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Located in the Beta Quadrant, Romulus is a Class M planet rich in vegetation, thanks to its temperate ecosystems and numerous bodies of water. Although it was not the Romulans’ original birthplace, they have inhabited the planet long enough to call it home, building vast cities known for their breathtaking architecture.\n"
"\n"
"Descendants of the Vulcans, the Romulans split from them and rejected the path of logic in favor of retaining their emotions. This divergence led them to found their own empire on two twin planets—Romulus and Remus."

msgid "IDS_PCZC926_STAR_TREK_2_3"
msgstr "Planet Qo'noS"

msgid "IDS_PCZC926_STAR_TREK_2_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Qo'noS, the Klingon homeworld, is a Class M planet with a thick atmosphere and harsh climate—ideally suited to its warrior inhabitants, who find honor in enduring rugged conditions and are not afraid of facing challenges.\n"
"\n"
"The planet's capital, First City, is the center of Klingon's political and military power. It's home to the Great Hall, where the Klingon High Council meets. It was here that Captain Picard completed Gowron's Rite of Succession in 2367."

msgid "IDS_PCZC927_STAR_TREK_2_4"
msgstr "Planet Earth"

msgid "IDS_PCZC927_STAR_TREK_2_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Located in the Sol system, Earth is a Class M planet with a diverse range of ecosystems. A home for humanity, Earth was once torn by wars and conflicts but managed to subsequently evolve into a symbol of peace, unity, and exploration. As a testament to lessons learned in the conflicts, by 2150, the United Earth was formed. It then became a founding member of the United Federation of Planets in 2161.\n"
"\n"
"As a key planet in the Federation, Earth plays a crucial role in galactic diplomacy."

msgid "IDS_PCZC928_STAR_TREK_3_1"
msgstr "Bat'leth"

msgid "IDS_PCZC928_STAR_TREK_3_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Bat'leth, also known as the Sword of Kahless, is a traditional Klingon weapon renowned for its conspicuous design—two curved blades and a central grip.\n"
"\n"
"The Bat'leth represents bravery and the pursuit of glory in battle, and it has deep cultural significance. Bat'leths are passed down through generations, and their use is often accompanied by rituals that emphasize the importance of skill, honor, and respect for one's rivals."

msgid "IDS_PCZC929_STAR_TREK_3_2"
msgstr "Borg Arm Weapon"

msgid "IDS_PCZC929_STAR_TREK_3_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Borg arm weapon is a unique, arm-mounted, directed energy weapon. Unlike standard Borg tools used for assimilation, this weapon fires energy bolts from the top of the forearm and is activated simply by pointing it at a target. This design allows for quick, precise attacks.\n"
"\n"
"The crew of U.S.S. Enterprise encountered a group of rogue Borg armed with these weapons. No longer seeking to assimilate others, these Borg pursued a different agenda—challenging both the Federation and their former Collective."

msgid "IDS_PCZC930_STAR_TREK_3_3"
msgstr "Type 2 Phaser"

msgid "IDS_PCZC930_STAR_TREK_3_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"With its sleek, ergonomic design, this phaser fires controlled energy bursts, allowing for precise, targeted shots. When set to non-lethal modes, it is used for stunning adversaries.\n"
"\n"
"This sidearm was a standard issue for Starfleet and United Federation of Planets personnel, both aboard starships and during away missions. Its versatility and ease of use made it a favored tool, especially in unpredictable situations."

msgid "IDS_PCZC931_STAR_TREK_3_4"
msgstr "Disruptor"

msgid "IDS_PCZC931_STAR_TREK_3_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Romulan disruptor pistols are the weapons of choice for Romulan military and intelligence operatives, delivering powerful energy blasts capable of inflicting serious damage or causing disintegration.\n"
"\n"
"Efficient in both close combat and precision attacks, these pistols feature various power settings but are generally engineered for more devastating outcomes."

msgid "IDS_PCZC932_STAR_TREK_4_1"
msgstr "Borg Queen"

msgid "IDS_PCZC932_STAR_TREK_4_1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The beginning, the end, and the mistress of the Hive mind—the Borg Queen is an enigma at the heart of the Collective.\n"
"\n"
"Unlike the drones she commands, the Queen has the autonomy to manipulate and deceive in order to assimilate. Through assimilation, the Borg grow stronger, integrating biological diversity and technological advancements of every new species they conquer to the Collective. As the strategic mind behind this pursuit, the Queen is focused on one ultimate goal—achieving perfection."

msgid "IDS_PCZC933_STAR_TREK_4_2"
msgstr "Worf"

msgid "IDS_PCZC933_STAR_TREK_4_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Worf—son of Mogh and a member of the esteemed House of Martok—is a formidable warrior who embraces the honor and strength of his Klingon heritage while upholding the principles of Starfleet.\n"
"\n"
"Raised by humans from a young age, Worf frequently reflects on questions of identity, loyalty, and the intricate balance between his Klingon roots and Starfleet's ideals, striving to honor both paths. A perfect example of his readiness to uphold the highest standards is his daring rescue of Captain Picard from the Borg cube."

msgid "IDS_PCZC934_STAR_TREK_4_3"
msgstr "TR-580 Tricorder"

msgid "IDS_PCZC934_STAR_TREK_4_3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Tricorders are versatile handheld sensor devices used for various "
"applications. Over the years, Starfleet's engineering and scientific "
"divisions developed and released numerous models, including the TR-580, used"
" by Starfleet personnel during the late 24th century. Primarily employed for"
" scientific study and analysis, tricorders featured one function that was "
"particularly helpful in emergencies. Starfleet personnel in distress could "
"press the EMRG button to transmit all data stored in the tricorder's memory "
"to the connected ship, facilitating rapid communication and information "
"sharing in a critical situation."

msgid "IDS_PCZC935_STAR_TREK_4_4"
msgstr "Sela"

msgid "IDS_PCZC935_STAR_TREK_4_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Sela, the daughter of Tasha Yar, a former officer of Starfleet, is an influential figure within the Romulan Empire. Since early childhood, Sela has carried the weight of complex issues such as loyalty, betrayal, and subterfuge. Driven by a desire for power, she often employs her sharp intellect and ruthless tactics to navigate the treacherous waters of Romulan politics.\n"
"\n"
"As a high-ranking officer in the Romulan military, Sela leverages her unique background to undermine her adversaries and exploit their vulnerabilities."

