msgid "IDS_PJSB719_COMPONENT_06_MINI_DOCKYARD_COMPONENT"
msgstr "Navigation Equipment"

msgid "IDS_PJSB719_DESCR"
msgstr ""
"A powerful battlecruiser design based on concepts created in Japan in "
"response to the ambitious U.S. shipbuilding program of 1919. She was "
"intended to be a ship of approximately 50,000 tons, capable of 30 knots, and"
" armed with guns of 410 mm or higher caliber. However, the Washington Naval "
"Conference prevented the implementation of these designs."

msgid "IDS_PJSB719_FULL"
msgstr "Hotaka"

msgid "IDS_PJSB719_NUMBER"
msgstr "1"

msgid "IDS_PJSB719_YEAR"
msgstr "1921"

msgid "IDS_PJSB720"
msgstr "Aki"

msgid "IDS_PJSB720_DESCR"
msgstr ""
"A large hybrid battleship and a hypothetical option considered for "
"converting a Yamato-class battleship into an aircraft-carrying ship. After "
"the loss of four aircraft carriers at Midway in 1942, Japan found itself in "
"desperate need of new ships of this type. At the same time, the prospect of "
"a classic major engagement between battle fleets was becoming increasingly "
"unlikely. In these circumstances, following the 1944 conversion of the Ise-"
"class ships into hybrid battleships, it was conceivable that more powerful "
"and modern battleships might also have been converted."

msgid "IDS_PJSB720_FULL"
msgstr "Aki"

msgid "IDS_PJSB720_NUMBER"
msgstr "1"

msgid "IDS_PJSB720_YEAR"
msgstr "1945"

msgid "IDS_PJSB730"
msgstr "Tōgasa"

msgid "IDS_PJSB730_DESCR"
msgstr ""
"A battlecruiser armed with 310 mm and 100 mm gun mounts originally intended "
"for the B-65 super cruiser design of 1941. The ship herself, designed in the"
" late 1910s, could have been built as part of the famous 8-8 Program and "
"modernized two decades later, with her armament replaced by more modern "
"artillery systems that were then in the design stage."

msgid "IDS_PJSB730_FULL"
msgstr "Tōgasa"

msgid "IDS_PJSB730_NUMBER"
msgstr "1"

msgid "IDS_PJSB730_YEAR"
msgstr "1941"

