msgid "IDS_PRSD709_YEAR"
msgstr "1955"

msgid "IDS_PRSD710"
msgstr "Peredovoy"

msgid "IDS_PRSD710_DESCR"
msgstr ""
"A Project 48 (Kiev-class) destroyer. Construction of the class started before the outbreak of World War II. Following the end of the conflict, the Soviet Navy sought to apply lessons learned during the war—primarily focusing on the importance of anti-aircraft weaponry. Plans were made to modernize the ships with the best anti-aircraft systems the Soviet Navy could provide.\n"
"\n"
"However, concerns about potential stability issues together with competition from newer Project 30-bis destroyers led to the cancellation of this modernization program. All work was ceased in 1950, and the two partially completed ships were later expended in post-war anti-ship missile tests."

msgid "IDS_PRSD710_FULL"
msgstr "Peredovoy"

msgid "IDS_PRSD710_NUMBER"
msgstr "1"

msgid "IDS_PRSD710_YEAR"
msgstr "1944"

msgid "IDS_PRSD718"
msgstr "Provorny"

msgid "IDS_PRSD718_DESCR"
msgstr ""
"One of the Type 1936A destroyers—unusual ships equipped with \"cruiser-"
"like\" main battery guns. Commissioned into the Kriegsmarine in "
"February 1943 as Z-33, she participated in military operations in the Arctic"
" and Norway during World War II. After the war, in late 1945, she was "
"transferred to the U.S.S.R. as part of war reparations and renamed Provorny."
" The destroyer served in the Baltic Sea until 1956 before getting disarmed "
"in 1958 and decommissioned in 1961."

msgid "IDS_PRSD718_FULL"
msgstr "Provorny"

msgid "IDS_PRSD718_NUMBER"
msgstr "15"

msgid "IDS_PRSD718_YEAR"
msgstr "1943"

msgid "IDS_PRSD810"
msgstr "DD R-10"

msgid "IDS_PRSD810_DESCR"
msgstr "Test ship."

msgid "IDS_PRSD810_FULL"
msgstr "DD R-10"

msgid "IDS_PRSD810_NUMBER"
msgstr "1"

msgid "IDS_PRSD810_YEAR"
msgstr "1940"

msgid "IDS_PRSD909"
msgstr "Neustrashimy B"

msgid "IDS_PRSD909_DESCR"
msgstr ""
"Adopted in 1945, a 10-year military shipbuilding program envisaged building "
"226 \"standard\" destroyers. Some of them were to fall under Project 30bis, "
"which had been successfully accommodated by the industrial sector, while "
"others were designated a new class. In 1949, the new lead ship of "
"Project 41, Neustrashimy, was laid down at the Zhdanov yard in Leningrad. A "
"total of 110 destroyers were planned to be built, but the series production "
"of such a complex ship was canceled in favor of the Project 56 destroyers."

msgid "IDS_PRSD909_FULL"
msgstr "Neustrashimy B"

msgid "IDS_PRSD909_NUMBER"
msgstr "1"

msgid "IDS_PRSD909_YEAR"
msgstr "1955"

